<title>SWEDEN: Stora posts big drop in '96 profit.</title>
<headline>Stora posts big drop in '96 profit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish forestry group Stora on Wednesday released its results for calendar 1996.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 2,349    vs  8,020</p>
<p> Turnover				  45,161    vs 57,106</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	   4.85    vs  16.70</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	    3.75    vs   3.75</p>
<p> Operating costs			 38,777    vs 44,785</p>
<p> One-off items		    CHARGE   37    vs    301 CREDIT</p>
<p> Depreciation			     3,488    vs  3,648</p>
<p> Operating profit			 2,859    vs  8,974</p>
<p> Net financial items	    CHARGE  510    vs    954 CHARGE</p>
<p> Tax					    770    vs  2,605</p>
<p> Minorities				    19    vs     48</p>
<p> Net income				 1,560    vs  5,367</p>
<p> Equity/assets ratio (pct)		 48    vs     47.6</p>
<p>NOTE - A Reuters poll of 16 analysts found the market expected Stora to report a profit after financial items of 2.55 billion crowns for 1996 and dividend payment of 3.30 crowns.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
